+## 2026-06-09 (Operational retrospective — milestone 2026.06.367)
+
+- Wrote `results/operational_retro_2026_06_367.json` (schema `carnot.operational_retro.v64`). Per the authoritative milestone-scoped timing block: 0 experiment commits since activation, 0 compute-bound experiments, 0 wall-clock minutes; both RTX 3090s idle at 0% util — correct behaviour (no compute-bound task), so `gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null` and GPU idle is NOT flagged.
+- **Finding (recurring): the zero-count is a milestone->commit detection gap, not an empty milestone.** The .367 changelog window contains real committed work (ARC-AGI-3 incremental solves, the GAP-3 Stage-1/Stage-2 verifier program, the capstone). This is the 4th consecutive false zero-count (.363/.365/.366/.367); the .366 retro already flagged the same contradiction. Highest-leverage action: repair the timing harness's commit detection/windowing (audit the activation-boundary SHA + the artifact filename match), add a self-check that diffs the detector count against a direct git-range artifact count and stamps `detector_gap_suspected` on disagreement, and backfill the timing analysis over .363-.367 once fixed. `estimated_time_savings_pct=0` (no measured wall-time exists to optimize — would be fabricated otherwise).
